<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom falls away as sellers meet buyback.</title>
<headline>Telecom falls away as sellers meet buyback.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in New Zealand market leader Telecom shed NZ 18 cents to NZ$6.32 within half an hour of trade on Thursday, as selling to meet the company's buyback programme dominated sentiment.</p>
<p>Brokers said the stock had been punished since reporting a disappointing third quarter result last week, and could well continue its slide.</p>
<p>The company said last November it planned a NZ$1 billion share repurchase programme over one year, starting in the fourth quarter of its 1996/97 fiscal year.  </p>
<p>Half the shares would be purchased on the New Zealand and New York Stock Exchanges and the other half directly from Ameritech and Bell Atlantic, which each own a quarter of the company.</p>
